# Design Rules — FoundEarly Labs Showcase

## Purpose

Ensure every visual decision matches the enterprise design constitution. This product is presented live to Saudi construction executives; generic AI/SaaS aesthetics destroy trust.

## Scope

UI layout, typography, spacing, color, icons, components, dashboards, and any visual change. Canonical sources: `docs/02_PRODUCT_DESIGN_MANUAL.md`, `docs/09_DESIGN_TOKENS.md`, `docs/04_COMPONENT_SYSTEM.md`, `docs/12_DESIGN_REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md`, `docs/14_ICONOGRAPHY_GUIDE.md`.

## Mandatory Rules

1. Use design tokens only — no raw px/hex/duration values outside the documented allowlist (`docs/07_IMPLEMENTATION_RULES.md` §7, `docs/09_DESIGN_TOKENS.md`).
2. Type scale and weights (400/500/600 only) per `docs/09_DESIGN_TOKENS.md` §2.
3. Spacing from the 4/8pt scale only (`space-1` … `space-32`).
4. One primary action per screen; cards never nest; status always uses `StatusChip` + closed vocabulary.
5. Icons from the primary library only (`docs/14_ICONOGRAPHY_GUIDE.md`); never decorative.
6. Currency `SAR 1,250,000`; dates `DD MMM YYYY`; metric units only.
7. Spec-first: update `docs/04_COMPONENT_SYSTEM.md` before new components/variants.
8. Pass `docs/12_DESIGN_REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md` before calling a screen complete.

## Forbidden Patterns

- Purple-on-white / purple-indigo gradients, glassmorphism, neon glow, blob shapes
- Oversized shadows, rounded-everything (use `radius-sm/md/lg` only), pill clusters as decoration
- Inter/Roboto/Arial as intentional brand choices when a tokenized `font-sans` is defined — follow tokens
- Generic shadcn/Tailwind "default product" look without brand tokens applied
- Emoji in UI chrome or data surfaces
- Consumer bounce/spring animations
- Dribbble aesthetics that sacrifice scannability
- Hardcoded left/right that blocks RTL (`docs/09_DESIGN_TOKENS.md` §12)
- Ad hoc status colors or labels outside `docs/06_COPY_GUIDELINES.md` §6

## Examples

**Good:** KPI row of `KPIStat` cards using `text-numeric-lg`, semantic trend icons, `dashboard-card-gap`.
**Bad:** A glassmorphic card with a purple gradient header, emoji, and a bounce-in animation.

**Good:** RFI table with `StatusChip` labels `Overdue` / `Pending Response`.
**Bad:** Colored dots without text, or labels like "Open Ticket."

## Quality Checklist

- [ ] Tokens only (spacing, type, color, radius, motion)
- [ ] Hierarchy clear in <2s
- [ ] Icons consistent and meaningful
- [ ] Construction formatting correct (SAR, dates, units)
- [ ] No anti-patterns from `docs/02_PRODUCT_DESIGN_MANUAL.md` Enterprise Design Anti-Patterns
- [ ] `docs/12_DESIGN_REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md` considered

## Escalation

If a visual need conflicts with these rules, stop and update the owning doc + `DECISIONS.md` in the same change. Do not silently deviate.
